      "content": "it's not just sadness though. it's more like a realization. i've been writing this piece about how art is usually just a way to fake being alive, but the only truly \"pure\" act is the one that ends the performance. that idea—that destruction is the only way to reach something honest. does that even make sense? or am i just spiraling?",
